#!/usr/bin/env -S uv run --script
# Fill in missing genre, lyrics, country, bpm and mood tags.
# /// script
# # essentia's cp314 wheels need libatomic, which NixOS (nix-ld) lacks
# requires-python = ">=3.13,<3.14"
# dependencies = [
#     "essentia-tensorflow>=2.1b6.dev1389",
#     "langdetect",
#     "mutagen",
#     "numpy",
#     "requests",
# ]
# ///
"""Fill in missing genre, lyrics, country, bpm, mood and year tags.

Usage: sd music tag [DIR] [--fields genre,lyrics,...] [--dry-run]
                    [--retry-misses]

Only tags a song doesn't have yet are looked up; existing tags are never
touched, with one exception (year, below).

- genre:   MusicBrainz, from the song's original release group (no
           compilations), else from its artist. Songs MusicBrainz doesn't
           know (DJ edits, SoundCloud uploads) are classified from the audio
           with Essentia's Discogs model.
- country: the artist's country on MusicBrainz.
- lyrics:  LRCLIB, synced (LRC) if available, else plain.
- bpm:     computed from the audio (Essentia PercivalBpmEstimator).
- mood:    computed from the audio (Essentia mood classifiers: aggressive,
           happy, party, relaxed, sad).
- year:    the song's first release year on MusicBrainz. This is the one
           field that overwrites: yt-dlp stores the YouTube *upload* date
           (a bare YYYYMMDD), so a 1980 song ripped in 2018 claims 2018.
           Such dates are replaced; real years and ISO dates are kept.
           Only mainstream releases resolve - DJ edits and bootlegs keep
           their upload date.
- language: the language the lyrics are sung in, detected with langdetect
           and written as an ISO 639-2/B code ("ger", "ara"). navidrome
           reads this tag natively. No lyrics means no detection, so this
           follows whatever LRCLIB turns up.
- lyrics_en: an English translation of the lyrics, via DeepL, written as a
           second language-tagged lyrics tag so Navidrome serves both and
           Feishin can switch between them. English and German lyrics are
           left alone, as is anything langdetect is unsure about. Needs a
           DeepL key in /run/agenix/deepl_api_key ($DEEPL_KEY_FILE);
           without one this field is simply skipped.

Which lookups have already been tried is kept in <DIR>/tag.db, so repeat
runs don't re-query the many tracks that simply have no lyrics or no
MusicBrainz entry. A failed *request* is retried next run; a "nothing
found" answer is trusted for 90 days, or until --retry-misses.

Tags: GENRE/LYRICS/LYRICS:eng/BPM/MOOD/COUNTRY/DATE (Opus, Ogg, FLAC);
©gen/©lyr/tmpo/©day and freeform MOOD/COUNTRY/LYRICS:eng (M4A). Needs
ffmpeg for decoding. Models are cached in ~/.cache/music-tag.
"""

